    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_MissionBody">Adam CodexHub is an independent, open-source project (MIT) created for everyone who wants to understand how Codex can work with many AI providers — without breaking the official sign-in, without exposing keys, and without a paywall.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_Step1Lead">Explore providers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_Step1Rest">Open the hub and see every provider as a first-class citizen — presets, keys, health, models.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_Step2Lead">Test before you trust.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_Step2Rest">Run streaming, tool-calling and structured-output probes with a live progress window — learn what each model can really do.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_Step3Lead">Read the source.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_Step3Rest">Cleanly layered: App → Core → Providers → Codex → Gateway. Each layer teaches one idea (DPAPI, adapters, transactional config, loopback routing).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_Step4Lead">Make it yours.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_Step4Rest">MIT license — fork it, study it, and ship your own ideas freely.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_About_FreeBody">No subscriptions, no trials, no token metering. Adam CodexHub is free forever — you only ever pay your own AI providers directly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec1">1 · HOW ADAM CODEXHUB FITS TOGETHER</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec1Body">The diagram below is generated from the repository itself: the WPF app and CLI talk to a clean Core; Providers wrap each AI service; Codex writes your config.toml safely; and a loopback Gateway lets Codex Desktop/CLI reach your chosen provider — keys never leave the machine in plaintext.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec2">2 · CHOOSE PROVIDER (HOME)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec2Lead">Pick the provider you want to use with Codex.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec2Rest"> Each provider shows its logo, health (Healthy / Warning / Unknown), the number of enabled models and its key status.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B2_1Lead">Add an API key</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B2_1Rest"> if the provider has none — keys are encrypted with Windows DPAPI.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B2_2Lead">Double-click a provider</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B2_2Rest"> to activate it with Codex (opens Desktop or CLI depending on the W / CLI badge).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B2_3Lead">Codex Account</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B2_3Rest"> restores the original sign-in — your keys and models are kept.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B2_4Lead">Show all providers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B2_4Rest"> toggles between providers you have configured and every built-in preset.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec3">3 · PROVIDERS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B3_1Lead">New / Refresh</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B3_1Rest"> manage the provider list.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B3_2Lead">Status column</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B3_2Rest"> — Unknown means the provider has not been health-checked yet; add a key and test to refresh it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B3_3Lead">Choose logo</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B3_3Rest"> picks a custom avatar for a provider (PNG/JPG up to 512 KB).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec4">4 · MODELS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B4_1Lead">Scan models</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B4_1Rest"> discovers what the provider exposes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B4_2Lead">Test a model</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B4_2Rest"> opens a live progress window — streaming, tool calling and structured JSON are probed in real time with the parameters each probe returned.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B4_3Lead">Enable / Disable</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_B4_3Rest"> decides what Codex may actually use. Only verified models should be enabled.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec5">5 · SESSIONS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_S5Prefix">Prepare a </sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_S5Lead">provider-safe project handoff</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_S5Rest">: point at a project directory, pick the target provider, and generate a continuation instruction — without editing Codex's internal session database.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec6">6 · DIAGNOSTICS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_S6Prefix">Check the </sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_S6Lead">local gateway</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_S6Rest"> and config recovery status: is the loopback proxy listening, is the token valid, were there rollbacks?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Sec7">7 · SETTINGS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_S7Body">Global preferences for how the hub behaves.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_TipsTitle">QUICK TIPS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Tip1">A provider can stay at Unknown until you test a key or run a model probe — that is normal.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Tip2">When a key hits a 429 or quota limit, the hub fails over to the next healthy key in that provider's pool (max 3 attempts).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Tip3">Every config change is backed up first — if anything breaks, Codex Account mode restores your original configuration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_Guide_Tip4">Free forever. You only pay your AI providers directly, never the hub.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_FR_Sec1Body">Adam CodexHub does not convert an existing chat session from one provider into another. Current project files, Git state and synchronized project state take priority over old chat history. Cross-provider use requires a separate session and a project handoff. A normal app exit restores the preserved Codex Account configuration; a crash or forced termination may prevent restoration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_FR_Sec2Body">When you use a remote provider, prompts, source code, files, outputs and metadata may be sent to that provider. Its terms, privacy policy, retention, training and cross-border transfer rules apply. Do not send confidential, personal or regulated data unless you are authorized and the provider is suitable.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_FR_Sec3Body">Key tests, model compatibility probes, retries and failover make real API requests and may consume credits or incur charges. Keys are protected at rest with Windows DPAPI, but no local tool can protect them from malicious software running as the same Windows user. Remote custom endpoints must use HTTPS; HTTP is allowed only for loopback providers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_FR_Sec4Body">This independent MIT-licensed project is intended for learning, experimentation and developer evaluation. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by OpenAI, Microsoft, GitHub or any provider, and it is not certified for safety-critical, regulated or other high-risk use.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_FR_Check1">I understand that providers may use separate sessions and that project state may be synchronized for handoff.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_FR_Check2">I understand that remote providers may receive my data and apply their own terms and privacy practices.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L10n_FR_Check3">I understand that probes and retries may cost money, and that I am responsible for provider charges, credentials, data and lawful use.</sys:String>
